          "ruleId": "DS111237",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies data into a destination buffer whose actual size is not known at this point in the code. The number of bytes to copy is determined by a variable (len-1), but there is no evidence that this value is properly bounded by the actual size of the destination buffer. This can lead to buffer overflows if len is greater than the buffer's capacity. Additionally, there is no explicit null-termination of the destination buffer after the copy, which can result in unterminated strings. The source is a C-style string, which is safe from overlap issues, and both the source and destination are not null at this point, but the main risk remains due to the lack of capacity checks.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo mitigate the risk of buffer overflow, ensure that the number of bytes copied does not exceed the actual size of the destination buffer. If possible, determine the size of the destination buffer and use it to limit the copy operation. Additionally, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer after copying to prevent unterminated string issues.\n\nFor example, if you know the maximum size of `version` (e.g., `VERSION_MAX_LEN`), you can do:\n\n```cpp\nstd::strncpy(version, empty.c_str(), VERSION_MAX_LEN - 1);\nversion[VERSION_MAX_LEN - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\nIf the size is dynamic and passed as `len`, ensure that `len` does not exceed the actual buffer size:\n\n```cpp\nsize_t safe_len = std::min(len, (int)ACTUAL_BUFFER_SIZE);\nstd::strncpy(version, empty.c_str(), safe_len - 1);\nversion[safe_len - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\nAlways validate that the length used for copying is within the bounds of the destination buffer, and explicitly null-terminate the buffer after copying.\n\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_overflow)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
