          "message": {
            "text": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the code uses a string copy function where the source and destination buffers may overlap in memory. This can lead to undefined behavior according to the C standard, as the function does not support overlapping memory regions. The analysis detected a feasible data flow from the destination to the source, indicating a real risk of overlap. Additionally, there are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent this scenario, and the source may also be null, which further increases the risk. The destination buffer's capacity is not explicitly known, and there is no evidence that the length argument is derived from the destination's actual size. All these factors contribute to the assessment that this is a genuine and actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the risk of undefined behavior caused by overlapping source and destination buffers in the string copy operation, ensure that the source and destination do not overlap. If overlap is possible, use `memmove` instead of `strncpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping memory regions safely. Additionally, always check that the source pointer is not null before performing the copy to avoid null pointer dereference.\n\n**Example fix:**\n\n```cpp\nif (brand != nullptr && info->vram_vendor != brand) {\n    strncpy(info->vram_vendor, brand, AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\n    info->vram_vendor[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n}\n```\n\nOr, if overlap is possible:\n\n```cpp\nif (brand != nullptr) {\n    memmove(info->vram_vendor, brand, AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\n    info->vram_vendor[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n}\n```\n\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_overflow)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
