          "ruleId": "DS140021",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Detected Vulnerability in C Function (strlen)",
            "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `strlen()` function in C and C++ is used to find the length of a string. However, it can lead to vulnerabilities if not used properly. The function counts the number of characters in a string until it reaches a null character (`'\\0'`). If the string is not null-terminated, `strlen()` will continue reading memory until it encounters a null character, potentially leading to buffer overflows, memory corruption, and other undefined behavior.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, `strlen(info.container_name) > 0`, the vulnerability arises if `info.container_name` is not a null-terminated string. This could lead to a buffer overflow vulnerability, where the `strlen()` function reads beyond the intended memory area.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, ensure that all strings are null-terminated. This can be done by initializing strings with a null character or by manually adding a null character at the end of the string after it has been modified.\n\nAlso, consider using safer alternatives to `strlen()`, such as `strnlen()`, which takes an additional parameter specifying the maximum number of characters to read. This can prevent buffer overflows by ensuring that `strlen()` does not read beyond the intended memory area.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace `strlen(info.container_name) > 0` with `info.container_name[0] != '\\0'`. This checks if the first character of the string is not a null character, which is a safer way to check if the string is empty.\n\n```cpp\nif (info.container_name[0] != '\\0') {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `strlen()` function is part of the C standard library, so no additional libraries are needed for the provided code snippet.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C/C++ Vulnerabilities](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_SCP_Quick_Reference_Guide_v2.pdf)\n- [CWE-126: Buffer Over-read](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/126.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/amd_smi/fdinfo.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 212,
                  "startColumn": 8,
                  "endLine": 212,
                  "endColumn": 35,
                  "charOffset": 7668,
                  "charLength": 27,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "strlen(info.container_name)",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "strlen(info.container_name)",
                      "markdown": "`strlen(info.container_name)`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "If a string is missing a null terminator, strlen will read past the end of the buffer"
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/amd_smi/fdinfo.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 7668,
                        "charLength": 27
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "strlen_s(info.container_name, <size of info.container_name>)"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "If a string is missing a null terminator, strlen will read past the end of the buffer"
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/amd_smi/fdinfo.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 7668,
