            "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the code uses a string copy operation where the source and destination buffers may overlap, which is undefined behavior according to the C standard. The analysis detected that the source and destination may refer to overlapping memory regions due to data flow between them. Additionally, there is no evidence of explicit null-termination after the copy, and the source may be null at this point, increasing the risk. The destination buffer is a pointer with unknown capacity, and there is no guard or check to ensure safe operation. These factors indicate a real risk of undefined behavior, which can lead to unpredictable program behavior or security vulnerabilities.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the undefined behavior caused by possible overlap between the source and destination buffers in the string copy operation, use `memmove` instead of `strncpy`. The `memmove` function is specifically designed to handle overlapping memory regions safely. Additionally, ensure that the source and destination pointers are not null before performing the copy, and consider explicitly null-terminating the destination buffer if it is intended to be a string.\n\nExample fix:\n\n```cpp\nif (name != nullptr && proc_id != nullptr) {\n    memmove(name, proc_id, len);\n    // Optionally, ensure null-termination if 'name' is a string\n    if (len > 0) {\n        name[len - 1] = '\\0';\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_overflow)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/amd_smi/amd_smi.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 430,
                  "startColumn": 4,
                  "endLine": 430,
                  "endColumn": 31,
                  "charOffset": 16794,
                  "charLength": 27,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "strncpy(name, proc_id, len)",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "strncpy(name, proc_id, len)",
                      "markdown": "`strncpy(name, proc_id, len)`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "strncpy is dangerous, as if the source contains 'n' or more characters, it will not null terminate the destination."
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/amd_smi/amd_smi.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 16794,
