          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the destination buffer's capacity is not known at the point of the copy operation, and the length argument used for the copy is not proven to be safe. The code copies a string into a character buffer using a length value that may not correspond to the actual size of the destination buffer. This can lead to buffer overflows if the length exceeds the buffer's capacity. There are no explicit checks or guards to ensure that the length does not exceed the buffer size, and there is no evidence that the length is derived from the buffer's capacity. Additionally, there is no explicit null-termination after the copy, which can lead to unterminated strings. The source is a C-style string, which reduces the risk of overlap, but the main concern remains the potential for buffer overflow due to the unknown size of the destination buffer.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo mitigate the risk of buffer overflow, ensure that the length argument used in the copy operation does not exceed the actual size of the destination buffer. If the destination buffer's size is known, use it directly as the maximum length. Additionally, ensure that the destination buffer is null-terminated after the copy, as `strncpy` does not guarantee null-termination if the source string is longer than the specified length.\n\nFor example, if you know the size of `name` (e.g., `NAME_SIZE`), you can do the following:\n\n```cpp\nstrncpy(name, socket->get_socket_id().c_str(), NAME_SIZE - 1);\nname[NAME_SIZE - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\nIf the size is not known, consider passing the buffer size as an additional argument or using safer string copy functions such as `snprintf`:\n\n```cpp\nsnprintf(name, NAME_SIZE, \"%s\", socket->get_socket_id().c_str());\n```\n\nRefer to the following resources for more information:\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
