          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Problematic C function detected (memcpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in a memory copy operation. The destination and source expressions are derived from dataflow analysis, indicating that they may refer to overlapping memory, which can result in undefined behavior according to the C standard. Additionally, there are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent this overlap, and the source may also be null, which further increases the risk. The destination is not a pointer-based member, suggesting it is likely a local variable or a field, but this does not mitigate the risk of overlap. The use of a fixed count of 4 bytes does not guarantee safety if the regions overlap. Therefore, this issue should be addressed to prevent potential memory corruption or unpredictable program behavior.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior caused by overlapping memory regions in memory copy operations, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. The `memmove` function is specifically designed to handle overlapping source and destination regions safely. Replace the original call with:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4);\n```\n\nThis change ensures that the copy operation is performed correctly even if the source and destination memory regions overlap.\n\nFor more information, see:\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-123: Write-what-where Condition](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/123.html)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "rocm_smi/src/rocm_smi_binary_parser.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 140,
                  "startColumn": 4,
                  "endLine": 140,
                  "endColumn": 44,
                  "charOffset": 4406,
                  "charLength": 40,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)",
                      "markdown": "`memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "There are a number of conditions in which memcpy can introduce a vulnerability (mismatched buffer sizes, null pointers, etc.). More secure alternitives perform additional validation of the source and destination buffer"
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "rocm_smi/src/rocm_smi_binary_parser.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 4406,
                        "charLength": 40
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "memcpy_s(&pmmetrics_version, <size of &pmmetrics_version>,  &buf1[12],  4)"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "DevSkimSeverity": "BestPractice",
            "DevSkimConfidence": "High",
            "tags": [
              "API.DangerousAPI.ProblematicFunction"
            ]
          }
