        {
          "ruleId": "DS185832",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "\"Detected Use of Prohibited C Function (strcpy)\"",
            "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `strcpy` function in C++ is a standard library function that copies a string. However, it is considered unsafe because it does not check the size of the destination buffer, which can lead to buffer overflow vulnerabilities if the source string is larger than the destination buffer. This can lead to crashes, data corruption, and potentially code execution, making it a serious security risk.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should use safer string copy functions that include a length parameter. This allows the function to ensure that it does not write past the end of the buffer. Functions like `strncpy`, `strlcpy` or `memcpy` can be used instead, but they must be used correctly to ensure they are safe.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `strcpy` function with a safer function like `strncpy`. Here is how you can do it:\n\n```cpp\nchar name[10];\nstrncpy(name, \"ID_TA_RAS\", sizeof(name));\nname[sizeof(name) - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n```\n\nIn this example, `strncpy` will copy at most `sizeof(name)` characters into the `name` buffer. If the source string is longer than this, it will be truncated. The last line ensures that the string is null-terminated, which `strncpy` does not guarantee.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `<cstring>` library to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C++ Secure Coding Practices](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "example/amd_smi_drm_example.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 185,
                  "startColumn": 8,
                  "endLine": 185,
                  "endColumn": 33,
                  "charOffset": 6149,
                  "charLength": 25,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "strcpy(name, \"ID_TA_RAS\")",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "strcpy(name, \"ID_TA_RAS\")",
                      "markdown": "`strcpy(name, \"ID_TA_RAS\")`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "strcpy is frequently dangerous, as it will cause a buffer overflow if the source is larger than the destination."
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "example/amd_smi_drm_example.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 6149,
                        "charLength": 25
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "strcpy_s(name, <size of name>,  \"ID_TA_RAS\")"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "strcpy is frequently dangerous, as it will cause a buffer overflow if the source is larger than the destination."
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "example/amd_smi_drm_example.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
