          "ruleId": "DS185832",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "\"Detected Use of Prohibited C Function (strcpy)\"",
            "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `strcpy` function in C++ is a standard library function that copies a string. It is considered unsafe because it does not check the size of the destination buffer, which can lead to buffer overflow if the source string is larger than the destination buffer. This can cause a program to crash or, in the worst case, allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, use safer string copy functions that check the size of the destination buffer. These include `strncpy`, `strlcpy`, or `memcpy`. However, these functions can also be misused, so it's important to always ensure that the destination buffer is large enough to hold the source string and the null terminator.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `strcpy` function with a safer function, such as `strncpy`. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```cpp\nchar name[12];\nstrncpy(name, \"CP_MEC_JT2\", sizeof(name));\nname[sizeof(name) - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n```\n\nIn this code, `strncpy` copies up to `sizeof(name)` characters from the source string to the destination buffer. The last line ensures that the string is null-terminated, which is necessary because `strncpy` does not null-terminate the string if the source string is larger than or equal to the size of the destination buffer.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `<cstring>` library, which provides the `strcpy` and `strncpy` functions.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C++ Secure Coding Practices](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "example/amd_smi_drm_example.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 83,
                  "startColumn": 8,
                  "endLine": 83,
                  "endColumn": 34,
                  "charOffset": 3450,
                  "charLength": 26,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "strcpy(name, \"CP_MEC_JT2\")",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "strcpy(name, \"CP_MEC_JT2\")",
                      "markdown": "`strcpy(name, \"CP_MEC_JT2\")`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "strcpy is frequently dangerous, as it will cause a buffer overflow if the source is larger than the destination."
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "example/amd_smi_drm_example.cc"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "charOffset": 3450,
