          "ruleId": "DS161085",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Problematic C function detected (malloc)",
            "markdown": "This finding is classified as 'Likely Vulnerable' because the result of a malloc call is used as the destination in a strcpy operation without a preceding check for NULL. The absence of a null guard before the first use of the allocated pointer (dev_name) increases the risk of a null pointer dereference if malloc fails. The allocation size is computed as sizeof(char)*len, but there are no zero guards or overflow checks, and the pointer is immediately used in a memory operation. The presence of a cast does not mitigate the risk. The pointer is also returned from the function and passed to another call, but these do not reduce the risk of dereferencing a null pointer. Therefore, this is a genuine vulnerability.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent a null pointer dereference after a failed allocation, always check the result of malloc before using the allocated memory. For example, if your original code is:\n\n```c\nchar *dev_name = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char)*len);\nstrcpy(dev_name, src);\n```\n\nYou should add a null check immediately after the allocation:\n\n```c\nchar *dev_name = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char)*len);\nif (dev_name == NULL) {\n    // Handle allocation failure, e.g., return an error or clean up\n    return NULL;\n}\nstrcpy(dev_name, src);\n```\n\nThis ensures that if malloc fails and returns NULL, the program does not attempt to use the null pointer, preventing undefined behavior and potential security vulnerabilities.\n\nFor more information, see:\n- [OWASP C Secure Coding Practices: Memory Allocation](https://owasp.org/www-project-c-secure-coding-practices/#memory-allocation)\n- [CWE-690: Unchecked Return Value to NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/690.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "goamdsmi_shim/smiwrapper/amdsmi_go_shim.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 408,
                  "startColumn": 28,
                  "endLine": 408,
                  "endColumn": 47,
                  "charOffset": 23169,
                  "charLength": 19,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "malloc(sizeof(char)",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "malloc(sizeof(char)",
                      "markdown": "`malloc(sizeof(char)`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "c"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "If the value provided to malloc is the result of unsafe integer math, it can result in an exploitable condition. "
              },
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "goamdsmi_shim/smiwrapper/amdsmi_go_shim.c"
